Subject: [PATCH] technology: block newly-added rfkill devices while offline

A new controller can arrive unblocked while OfflineMode is true. Do not enable
its technology on ADD; request blocking and apply the confirmed CHANGE normally.
Still process the ADD's hard-block metadata: a newly usable controller can make
a previously fully hard-blocked technology available. Returning before updating
that metadata leaves the technology incorrectly hard-blocked with mixed devices.

Also suppress transient enabling when a hardware block is released while offline;
the existing hard-block-change path already requests a soft block in this case.
Preserve explicit soft-block power changes on existing controllers and persistent
policy outside offline mode. Propagate the new ADD blocking request's error.

Upstream-Status: Pending

--- a/src/technology.c
+++ b/src/technology.c
@@ -1764,8 +1764,9 @@
 					technology->softblocked) {
 		if (technology_disabled(technology) != -EALREADY)
 			technology_affect_devices(technology, false);
-	} else if (!technology->hardblocked &&
-					!technology->softblocked) {
+	} else if (!(global_offlinemode &&
+			(new_rfkill || hardblock_changed)) &&
+			!technology->hardblocked && !technology->softblocked) {
 		if (technology_enabled(technology) != -EALREADY)
 			technology_affect_devices(technology, true);
 	}
@@ -1825,6 +1826,8 @@
 				softblock, hardblock, true))
 		return 0;
 
+	if (global_offlinemode && !softblock)
+		return __connman_rfkill_block(type, true);
 	if (global_offlinemode)
 		return 0;
 
